(CLI-03: `--run` - compile and run the program in one command. The
 compiler's own stdout is the program's stdout; check-probes.sh's plain
 build-then-run form gives the same observable result, so the standard
 probe run below doubles as the --run hand-check.
 Hand-run separately:
   $ vox hello.vox --run
   Hello, World!
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox CLI-03.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   Hello, World!
)
Print "Hello, World!".
